  "description": "Captures one man spending a decade re-editing the entire century of cinema inside his own head. Eight parts of layered clips, paintings, text and whispered commentary: film history as a projection apparatus that showed everything and recognised almost nothing — your framework again, but as autobiography. The monument to close on; take it in parts, the way it was made.\n\nA cryptic message from Bond’s past sends him on a trail to uncover a sinister organization. While M battles political forces to keep the secret service alive, Bond peels back the layers of deceit to reveal the terrible truth behind SPECTRE.",
